65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: So, which option actually stops the mental math and the awkward money talks?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: Option A. A fixed seasonal rate removes the monthly shock. I can budget against a known figure, not a surprise.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: Option C. If we just split it evenly, there is no one to do the monthly logging. I keep my evenings.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,- **Shunichi**: Option B. The data proves the current split is broken. Meters end the guessing and the resentment.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: Option A. A fixed rate means no monthly demands, no late payments, and no awkward reminders. It protects our peace.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: I'm leaning toward A. If the rate is fixed, I can stop worrying about the bill and just live here comfortably.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: @Mio, I agree with A. The seasonal variance is too high for a flat monthly split, and I need that predictability.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Mio, but A still needs someone to do the year-end reconciliation. I saw how long that takes. I'm sticking with C.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"- **Shunichi**: @Rin, C ignores the four-to-one usage gap. B is the only option that actually fixes the math, not just the mood.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Shunichi, B requires an electrician and constant monitoring. A is the only choice that stops the arguments before they start.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,- **Mio**: I vote A. I want to stop calculating in my head and just live here without the winter anxiety.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,- **Ryuji**: I vote A. The seasonal fixed rate gives me the predictability I need to budget without the monthly shock.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I vote C. I refuse to be the one doing the year-end reconciliation. Even splits are the only way I keep my evenings free.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
